From: Prithwiraj Samanta <prskid1000@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 07:07:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] telecode: shader and mesh-gradient fills

A procedural fill is a CUSTOM paint (its colour is the fallback other readers
show) whose customEffectId links to a JSON definition in the node's shared
plugin data, telecode/fill:<id>, so both survive .fig. The renderer
(core canvas/gradients/procedural) paints kind "shader" as a Skia runtime
effect (SkSL half4 main(float2 p), u_size supplied, named uniforms; five
original presets) and kind "mesh" as one Coons patch per grid cell
(Catmull-Rom edges, warpable points, max 64) recorded into a picture shader;
a definition that does not compile paints the fallback. Compiled effects are
cached per CanvasKit and disposed with the renderer. telecode_fill_set /
_list / _remove / _presets edit them (shaders are compiled first and refused
with the compiler message).
